# The example carries no secrets and documents the flags, so it ships.
!.env.example
# SQLite, and the two sidecar files it writes next to every database. The
# trailing `*` is the point: `-wal` and `-shm` do not end in `.db`, so the
# plain patterns matched the database and let its write-ahead log through.
# That log is where SQLite keeps pages it has not checkpointed yet, so the
# demo conversations were being committed as binary churn, 1.8MB in one case.
*.sqlite*
*.sqlite3*
*.db*
.DS_Store

# Build output
web/dist/
api/dist/

# Held-out judging material. Shipped inside the provided pack and marked
# "do not ship to participants". Publishing it would leak the generalisation
# set for every team. Tests that use it skip when it is absent.
data/crew-ops-advisor-dataset/internal/

